    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0521" n="501" xml:id="pg501"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 23, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Recurring to the parts of your notes of
                    the 17th of July last,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d251-f1"/> and of the 31st of
                    October, which relate to the alleged cruel treatment of the master, mate, and
                    engineer of the British steamer Victor, at Fort Taylor, Key-West, I have the
                    honor to enclose, in reply, a copy of a communication of the 16th instant from
                    the War Department on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD. </signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Sc.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d251-a1.xml" xpointer="d251-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d251-a2.xml" xpointer="d251-a2"/>
            </div>
